00:40:13.500 --> 00:40:13.620
Yeah.
是啊。

714
00:40:13.720 --> 00:40:14.360
I just said it.
我刚才说了啊。

715
00:40:14.480 --> 00:40:17.560
Because there's one guy that's like, bing, bong, bong, bong, bong, bing, bong.
因为有一个人负责那种，叮，咚，咚，咚，咚，叮，咚。

716
00:40:17.640 --> 00:40:18.220
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

717
00:40:18.300 --> 00:40:18.500
Yeah.
明白。

718
00:40:18.620 --> 00:40:20.820
And then there's another person that's like, la, la, la.
然后另一个人负责那种，啦，啦，啦。

719
00:40:20.920 --> 00:40:21.680
Like, I don't get it.
就是，我搞不懂。

720
00:40:22.400 --> 00:40:23.720
But it sounded amazing.
但听起来真的很棒。

721
00:40:23.920 --> 00:40:25.440
I still can't believe he did that himself.
我还是不敢相信那是他自己完成的。

722
00:40:26.360 --> 00:40:31.620
One of the things I love about the scene, obviously, how much Andy's annoying everyone
我喜欢这个场景的原因之一，显然是安迪已经让每个人都感到厌烦了。

723
00:40:31.620 --> 00:40:32.100
already.
已经烦透了。

724
00:40:32.860 --> 00:40:35.180
But he calls Ryan big turkey.
但他管瑞安叫大火鸡。

725
00:40:35.960 --> 00:40:36.460
Yeah.
是啊。

726
00:40:36.820 --> 00:40:39.540
Does that mean that Ryan eats turkey sandwiches for lunch?
那是不是意味着瑞安午餐吃火鸡三明治？

727
00:40:39.700 --> 00:40:40.440
It has to.
肯定是。

728
00:40:40.760 --> 00:40:41.680
It has to.
肯定是。

729
00:40:41.940 --> 00:40:43.220
What are we learning here?
我们从中了解到了什么？

730
00:40:43.660 --> 00:40:47.360
Well, clearly, I mean, Andy had a friend called Broccoli Rob.
嗯，很明显，我是说，安迪有个朋友叫西兰花罗布。

731
00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:48.420
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

732
00:40:48.640 --> 00:40:48.880
Yes.
明白。

733
00:40:49.240 --> 00:40:51.080
All of the nicknames are just what you eat.
所有的绰号都是你吃的东西。

734
00:40:51.520 --> 00:40:52.020
Yeah.
是啊。

735
00:40:52.220 --> 00:40:53.140
I'm Yogurt Pam.
我是酸奶帕姆。

736
00:40:53.400 --> 00:40:54.640
I'd be Donut Kinsey.
我会是甜甜圈金西。

737
00:40:55.440 --> 00:40:56.620
Well, in real life.
嗯，在现实生活中。

738
00:40:56.720 --> 00:40:57.740
Oh, in real life.
哦，在现实生活中。

739
00:40:57.860 --> 00:40:58.080
Yes.
是的。

740
00:40:58.380 --> 00:41:00.780
I guess I'd be Eggs and Strawberries Fisher.
我想我会是鸡蛋草莓费舍尔。

741
00:41:01.600 --> 00:41:02.500
That's catchy.
那挺顺口的。

742
00:41:04.380 --> 00:41:11.640
Jenna, I feel like there is a very classic Jim-Pam shot that we have to talk about.
珍娜，我觉得有一个非常经典的吉姆和帕姆的镜头我们必须聊聊。

743
00:41:11.880 --> 00:41:12.620
What is it?
是什么？

744
00:41:12.720 --> 00:41:14.660
It's at 1 minute 58 seconds.
在1分58秒的时候。

745
00:41:15.220 --> 00:41:18.820
Andy is singing the ridiculous version of Andy and the tuna.
安迪在唱那个荒唐版的《安迪与金枪鱼》。

746
00:41:19.100 --> 00:41:19.920
You know, that whole part?
你知道，就是那整段？

747
00:41:20.300 --> 00:41:20.800
Yes.
知道。

748
00:41:21.080 --> 00:41:28.660
And the camera focuses on Jim's reaction and then pushes past Jim and Jim goes out of
镜头先是聚焦在吉姆的反应上，然后越过吉姆，吉姆变得模糊，镜头落在了帕姆身上。

749
00:41:28.660 --> 00:41:30.720
focus and it lands on Pam.
他们俩的表情如出一辙，就像在说，天哪，这家伙。

750
00:41:31.300 --> 00:41:36.960
And they both have similar expressions of like, oh, my God, this guy.
他们俩的表情如出一辙，就像在说，天哪，这家伙。

751
00:41:37.260 --> 00:41:39.440
And for me, I don't know.
至于我，我也不知道。

752
00:41:39.600 --> 00:41:43.180
I know I love Jim and Pam so much, so I don't know if I'm like looking for meaning.
我知道我非常喜欢吉姆和帕姆，所以我不知道自己是否在寻找什么深意。

753
00:41:43.180 --> 00:41:47.480
But in that moment, I'm like, they're on the same page.
但在那一刻，我觉得他们俩想法一致。

754
00:41:47.820 --> 00:41:50.220
These two are both in it.
这两个人都全身心投入其中。

755
00:41:50.380 --> 00:41:54.780
Like, they're going to be in it together for this episode because it's hitting them the
就像是，他们这一集要一起面对这件事，因为这件事对他们的影响是

756
00:41:54.780 --> 00:41:55.340
same way.
一样的。

757
00:41:56.160 --> 00:41:56.440
Yes.
没错。

758
00:41:56.640 --> 00:42:00.200
I think this is that first hint that they are in sync.
我觉得这是他们心意相通的第一个迹象。

759
00:42:00.500 --> 00:42:01.600
I think so.
我也这么认为。

760
00:42:01.700 --> 00:42:06.640
And it was just also a beautiful shot just to be a technical nerd.
而且作为一个技术宅，我得说那镜头拍得真美。

761
00:42:06.640 --> 00:42:08.220
Like, that is a beautiful shot.
真的，那镜头太美了。

762
00:42:08.380 --> 00:42:09.100
I agree.
我同意。

763
00:42:09.360 --> 00:42:13.440
Well, now Michael arrives to work and he's parked his car.
好了，现在迈克尔到了公司，停好了车。

764
00:42:13.620 --> 00:42:14.220
His, you know what?
他的，你知道吗？

765
00:42:14.300 --> 00:42:16.060
His roof won't go up, but who cares?
他的车顶关不上了，但谁在乎呢？

766
00:42:16.320 --> 00:42:16.760
It's fine.
没关系。

767
00:42:16.880 --> 00:42:17.700
He's going to leave it.
他打算就那样放着。

768
00:42:17.900 --> 00:42:18.040
Nope.
不。

769
00:42:18.060 --> 00:42:19.040
It's not going to be a problem.
那不会是个问题。

770
00:42:19.280 --> 00:42:21.280
It's not going to be a big deal on the biggest snow day they've had.
在他们经历过的最大的一场雪天里，这根本不算什么大事。

771
00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:23.600
I watched this episode with my kids.
我和我的孩子们一起看了这一集。

772
00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:24.680
I know I talked about that.
我知道我提过这件事。

773
00:42:24.880 --> 00:42:26.280
They loved his hair.
他们很喜欢他的发型。

774
00:42:26.600 --> 00:42:30.760
They loved how his hair was just messy from getting out of his car.
他们喜欢他从车里出来后那乱糟糟的头发。

775
00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:32.600
I didn't even notice that.
我甚至都没注意到这一点。

776
00:42:32.680 --> 00:42:33.860
That's such a good detail.
那真是个很棒的细节。

777
00:42:34.040 --> 00:42:34.460
I know.
我知道。

778
00:42:34.600 --> 00:42:34.800
I know.
我知道。

779
00:42:34.880 --> 00:42:35.820
They catch a few things.
他们总能发现一些细节。

780
00:42:35.820 --> 00:42:37.060
I'm going to sprinkle them through.
我会把这些发现穿插在节目里。

781
00:42:37.420 --> 00:42:38.700
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

782
00:42:39.120 --> 00:42:43.680
Well, Oscar arrives next to Michael and he is welcomed back by Michael.
好了，奥斯卡停在迈克尔旁边，迈克尔欢迎他回来。

783
00:42:43.920 --> 00:42:44.220
Yeah.
是啊。

784
00:42:44.400 --> 00:42:46.080
Michael says, hey, nice new car.
迈克尔说，嘿，不错的新车。

785
00:42:46.280 --> 00:42:51.880
And Oscar said, well, I got this new car in the settlement after you kissed me at work.
奥斯卡说，哦，这车是我在公司被你强吻后，通过和解协议买的。

786
00:42:52.340 --> 00:42:54.920
I love how matter-of-factly Oscar says it.
我喜欢奥斯卡说这话时那种不以为意的语气。

787
00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:57.860
That Lexus SUV, that's all you, buddy.
那辆雷克萨斯SUV，全靠你了，伙计。

788
00:42:58.580 --> 00:43:01.960
And then Michael's like, well, that's how we do it here at Dunder Mifflin.
然后迈克尔说，嗯，这就是我们在邓德·米夫林行事的方式。

789
00:43:02.060 --> 00:43:03.500
When we settle, we settle high.
我们要和解，就得要高额赔偿。

790
00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:04.440
Oh, God.
天哪。

791
00:43:05.160 --> 00:43:05.480
So.
所以。

792
00:43:07.410 --> 00:43:14.430
And then Oscar has that great talking head where he says part of him wants people in the office to have learned their lesson and to shut the hell up.
然后奥斯卡有一个很棒的采访镜头，他说他内心一部分希望办公室里的人能吸取教训，闭上那张臭嘴。

793
00:43:14.650 --> 00:43:18.330
But another part of him wants them to keep talking so he can buy a home theater.
但另一部分又希望他们继续说下去，这样他就能买得起家庭影院了。

794
00:43:19.390 --> 00:43:21.030
So now we go into Michael's office.
现在我们进入迈克尔的办公室。

795
00:43:21.190 --> 00:43:27.830
And Jenna, it's one of those classic scenes that you and I love where it starts with Michael and who else is in the room?
珍娜，这是你我都很喜欢的那种经典场景，开始时只有迈克尔，还有谁在房间里呢？

796
00:43:27.830 --> 00:43:28.650
You don't know.
你不知道。

797
00:43:28.830 --> 00:43:29.650
And then it's revealed.
然后真相大白。

798
00:43:29.890 --> 00:43:30.990
And this time it's Andy.
这次是安迪。

799
00:43:31.330 --> 00:43:35.090
Andy is taking the spot of Dwight over Michael's shoulder.
安迪取代了德怀特的位置，站在迈克尔身后。

800
00:43:35.090 --> 00:43:36.910
But he's creeping Michael out.
但他让迈克尔感到毛骨悚然。

801
00:43:37.050 --> 00:43:37.990
You can already tell.
你已经能看出来了。

802
00:43:38.450 --> 00:43:45.050
Well, there's a way that Michael is always kind of annoyed when Dwight interjects in the middle of what Michael is saying.
嗯，迈克尔总是因为德怀特在他说话时插嘴而感到有些恼火。

803
00:43:45.050 --> 00:43:46.590
But this is different.
但这回不一样。

804
00:43:47.250 --> 00:43:48.790
Like, Michael's annoyed by Dwight.
迈克尔对德怀特是那种恼火。

805
00:43:49.070 --> 00:43:52.410
But Michael, like, really is annoyed by Andy.
但迈克尔对安迪，是真的感到厌烦。

806
00:43:52.750 --> 00:43:54.570
Well, you know what it feels like to me?
嗯，你知道这给我的感觉是什么吗？

807
00:43:54.710 --> 00:43:56.990
Like, Andy is getting under his skin.
就像安迪让他感到很不舒服。

808
00:43:57.550 --> 00:43:59.070
Like, Dwight is like an annoying brother.
德怀特就像个烦人的兄弟。

809
00:43:59.070 --> 00:44:03.350
But Andy is like the creeper that lives down the street.
但安迪就像住在街那头的怪人。

810
00:44:03.590 --> 00:44:04.550
I don't know.
我不知道。

811
00:44:04.850 --> 00:44:07.110
That you try to avoid when you go to the mailbox.
就是那种你去邮箱取信时会尽量避开的人。

812
00:44:07.750 --> 00:44:12.890
Well, we had a fan question in this scene from Tennille who wants to know,
嗯，我们这一幕有个粉丝提问，来自Tennille，她想知道，

813
00:44:13.050 --> 00:44:18.210
in this episode, there are a lot of talking heads with Michael facing the window where it's snowing.
在这一集中，有很多迈克尔对着窗外下雪的场景进行的访谈。

814
00:44:18.390 --> 00:44:24.110
Were those talking heads shot in sequence so that they didn't have to keep turning the snow on and off?
这些访谈是按顺序拍摄的吗，这样就不用一直开关造雪机了？

815
00:44:25.610 --> 00:44:26.170
Yes.
是的。

816
00:44:26.790 --> 00:44:27.350
Yes.
没错。

817
00:44:27.350 --> 00:44:28.990
I love this question, Angela.
我喜欢这个问题，安吉拉。

818
00:44:29.070 --> 00:44:30.750
Because we've never really talked about this.
因为我们从来没真正聊过这个。

819
00:44:30.930 --> 00:44:34.950
We always shot all of our talking heads in a row.
我们总是把所有的访谈片段集中在一起拍摄。

820
00:44:35.410 --> 00:44:41.150
So what they would do is they would set up the shot, let's say, in Michael's office for a talking head.
所以他们会先布置好机位，比如在迈克尔的办公室里拍访谈。

821
00:44:41.290 --> 00:44:47.290
And every talking head he had for that episode, they would spend hours doing all of them.
然后他那一集里所有的访谈，他们会花上几个小时全部拍完。

822
00:44:47.430 --> 00:44:49.250
And the same thing in the conference room.
会议室里也是一样。

823
00:44:49.410 --> 00:44:55.510
Remember, they'd set up the chair and we would all cycle in for hours and do our talking heads.
记得吗，他们会摆好椅子，我们所有人轮流进去，花上几个小时拍完各自的访谈。

824
00:44:55.890 --> 00:44:56.090
Yes.
是的。

825
00:44:56.170 --> 00:44:58.830
It would literally be like talking head day on set.
那简直就是片场的“访谈日”。

826
00:44:59.470 --> 00:45:03.090
And I always really felt for Steve because he always had the moSt.
我总是很心疼史蒂夫，因为他的访谈最多。

827
00:45:03.310 --> 00:45:09.930
And I would think like, oh, my God, I had to like learn one, you know, and maybe they would give me some alts on the day.
我会想，天哪，我只需要背一段，你知道，也许当天他们还会给我一些备选台词。

828
00:45:10.370 --> 00:45:14.330
But Steve had to learn so many and just sit there and do them and do them.
但史蒂夫得背那么多台词，还得坐在那儿一遍又一遍地拍。

829
00:45:14.330 --> 00:45:17.450
And Veda would be there, our scripty, our script supervisor.
维达会在那儿，我们的场记，我们的剧本监督。

830
00:45:17.670 --> 00:45:20.990
And sometimes she would remind you if you had more than one.
有时候如果你有不止一段访谈，她会提醒你。

831
00:45:21.130 --> 00:45:24.110
Okay, now remember, this talking head is after Dwight left.
好了，记住，这段访谈是在德怀特离开之后拍的。

832
00:45:24.110 --> 00:45:27.110
So you're more sad than the one before, you know.
所以你要比上一段表现得更难过一点，你知道的。

833
00:45:27.350 --> 00:45:30.850
So sometimes she was helping us kind of navigate the time sequence of it all.
所以有时候她会帮我们理清整个时间线。

834
00:45:30.850 --> 00:45:31.850
So yes.
所以是的。

835
00:45:32.270 --> 00:45:38.590
And we would usually do these either first thing in the morning or at the end of the day.
我们通常会在清晨或者一天结束时拍这些。

836
00:45:38.850 --> 00:45:40.630
Steve would always do his first thing in the morning.
史蒂夫总是会在清晨先拍他的。

837
00:45:40.770 --> 00:45:42.290
I think he liked to lead with them.
我想他喜欢先处理这些。

838
00:45:42.650 --> 00:45:49.030
He would oftentimes, I feel like on a Monday, it would be like Steve talking heads until almost lunch.
我觉得通常在周一，史蒂夫几乎要拍一上午的访谈直到午饭时间。

839
00:45:49.030 --> 00:45:54.030
And then we would all come in and film like group scenes for the rest of the day.
然后我们所有人再进来，拍剩下的群戏。

840
00:45:54.850 --> 00:46:01.810
But then on Fridays, we would spend Friday afternoons all the rest of the cast doing our talking heads.
但周五下午，我们会花时间让其他演员拍完各自的访谈。

841
00:46:02.030 --> 00:46:03.890
That was kind of how we framed our week.
这就是我们安排一周工作的方式。

842
00:46:04.170 --> 00:46:05.570
Yeah, that's how I remember it, too.
没错，我也记得是这样。

843
00:46:06.070 --> 00:46:10.590
Well, Jenna, you know, Oscar's back now and he walks back over to accounting.
嗯，珍娜，你知道，奥斯卡现在回来了，他走回了会计部。

844
00:46:10.650 --> 00:46:15.210
And of course, Kevin has a ridiculous joke that he's been saving for weeks.
当然，凯文有个他憋了好几周的荒唐笑话。

845
00:46:15.610 --> 00:46:16.310
Kevin thought of it.
凯文想出来的。

846
00:46:16.410 --> 00:46:17.570
He was like, how was your gaycation?
他说，你的“同性假期”（gaycation）过得怎么样？

847
00:46:17.830 --> 00:46:18.610
Oscar's like, awesome.
奥斯卡说，棒极了。

848
00:46:19.030 --> 00:46:22.030
Kevin's like, yeah, I thought of that two seconds after you left.
凯文说，是啊，你刚走两秒我就想到了。

849
00:46:22.270 --> 00:46:23.750
Kevin's so proud of himself.
凯文对自己得意极了。

850
00:46:24.970 --> 00:46:27.110
And Angela is just like, hello.
而安吉拉的反应就是，你好。

851
00:46:27.330 --> 00:46:28.190
And he's like, hello.
然后他就说，你好。

852
00:46:28.470 --> 00:46:34.850
And you can tell that there's, I feel like a lot she wants to say, but she's not ready yet.
你可以感觉到，我觉得她有很多话想说，但还没准备好。

853
00:46:35.010 --> 00:46:36.230
She doesn't know how to say it yet.
她还不知道该怎么说。

854
00:46:36.590 --> 00:46:37.030
Yeah.
是啊。

855
00:46:37.250 --> 00:46:43.030
But then eventually, Angela does invite Oscar to join the party planning committee.
但最终，安吉拉还是邀请了奥斯卡加入派对策划委员会。

856
00:46:43.250 --> 00:46:47.330
She says she's sorry for the way certain things transpired.
她说她为某些事情的发生方式感到抱歉。

857
00:46:47.330 --> 00:46:48.930
And she wants to make some changes.
她想做出一些改变。

858
00:46:49.110 --> 00:46:50.370
And she starts crying.
然后她开始哭了起来。

859
00:46:51.070 --> 00:46:51.190
Yeah.
是啊。

860
00:46:52.430 --> 00:46:54.090
Well, Jenna, I really cried.
嗯，珍娜，我当时是真的哭了。

861
00:46:54.290 --> 00:46:55.830
That was me really crying.
那是我真实的哭泣。

862
00:46:55.830 --> 00:47:01.210
And I had a whole conversation with Greg about it as we were trying to find the scene.
在尝试拍摄那场戏时，我和格雷格就此进行了深入的交流。

863
00:47:01.210 --> 00:47:06.530
And I did one take, and he was like, Angela, I'm feeling sad.
