01:22:54.430 --> 01:22:57.730
fake pieces of plastic snow are going to fly out at them.
塑料假雪片就会喷到他们脸上。

1623
01:22:57.950 --> 01:22:58.210
Yes.
没错。

1624
01:22:58.490 --> 01:22:59.810
I loved that tidbit.
我太喜欢这个八卦了。

1625
01:23:00.010 --> 01:23:03.810
I loved that every time we tried to turn on the AC, snow would come out of there.
我喜欢他们每次开空调，雪就会喷出来的那种感觉。

1626
01:23:03.910 --> 01:23:06.210
Well, Michael has now, he's at Staples.
好了，迈克尔现在已经到了史泰博办公用品店。

1627
01:23:06.370 --> 01:23:07.790
He's going to go up to Dwight.
他要去找德怀特了。

1628
01:23:07.890 --> 01:23:08.770
He's going to apologize.
他要去道歉。

1629
01:23:08.770 --> 01:23:10.330
He wants him to come back.
他想让他回来。

1630
01:23:11.170 --> 01:23:14.510
And I love this scene so much.
我非常喜欢这一幕。

1631
01:23:14.670 --> 01:23:17.290
I mean, Dwight is tearing up.
我是说，德怀特都快哭了。

1632
01:23:17.510 --> 01:23:19.070
It is a very bromance moment.
这是一个非常“兄弟情”的时刻。

1633
01:23:19.070 --> 01:23:20.210
Well, yes.
嗯，是的。

1634
01:23:20.430 --> 01:23:22.570
That is what Greg calls it.
格雷格就是这么称呼它的。

1635
01:23:22.730 --> 01:23:24.930
He calls it the bromance moment.
他称之为“兄弟情”时刻。

1636
01:23:25.630 --> 01:23:32.470
And, you know, playing underneath this scene is the song from An Officer and a Gentleman.
而且，你知道，这一幕的背景音乐是《军官与绅士》里的那首歌。

1637
01:23:32.610 --> 01:23:32.990
Yes.
是的。

1638
01:23:33.150 --> 01:23:37.970
Remember at the end of Officer and a Gentleman where she's in the factory working and Richard
还记得《军官与绅士》结尾，她在工厂工作，理查·基尔

1639
01:23:37.970 --> 01:23:42.470
Gere walks in and he scoops her up and they kiss and everyone cheers?
走进来把她抱起，他们接吻，大家都在欢呼的那一幕吗？

1640
01:23:42.470 --> 01:23:44.370
It's, it's, it's, what is it?
那是，那是，那是，叫什么来着？

1641
01:23:44.450 --> 01:23:47.410
It's, it's, it's love lift us up where we belong.
是《爱让我们升华到属于我们的地方》。

1642
01:23:47.650 --> 01:23:47.910
Yes.
对。

1643
01:23:47.970 --> 01:23:48.050
Right?
是吧？

1644
01:23:48.210 --> 01:23:48.470
Yes.
是的。

1645
01:23:49.070 --> 01:23:50.650
Where the eagles fly.
雄鹰翱翔的地方。

1646
01:23:50.670 --> 01:23:50.930
Yes.
没错。

1647
01:23:51.210 --> 01:23:51.450
The whole thing.
整首歌都是。

1648
01:23:51.930 --> 01:23:58.490
Well, there is like a, a Muzak version of this playing at Staples during this scene.
这一幕在史泰博里播放的是这首歌的轻音乐版本。

1649
01:23:58.670 --> 01:23:59.370
It's amazing.
太棒了。

1650
01:23:59.730 --> 01:24:05.230
Guys, Greg sent in an audio clip talking about this bromance.
伙计们，格雷格发来了一段音频，谈论了这个兄弟情。

1651
01:24:05.230 --> 01:24:12.670
The ending of the return was like the big bromance moment between Michael and Dwight.
回归的那一幕就像迈克尔和德怀特之间那种伟大的兄弟情时刻。

1652
01:24:13.570 --> 01:24:17.710
I'm pretty sure the officer and a gentleman was in the script to begin with.
我很确定剧本里一开始就有《军官与绅士》那个桥段。

1653
01:24:18.070 --> 01:24:24.650
As I recall, we, we were building towards that moment to see Michael going through the aisles
我记得我们当时就在铺垫那个时刻，看着迈克尔穿过史泰博的过道，

1654
01:24:24.650 --> 01:24:30.250
at Staples and trying to, you know, make a big romantic moment out of it.
试图把它变成一个浪漫的大场面。

1655
01:24:30.250 --> 01:24:33.170
Like Richard Gere returning for Debra Winger.
就像理查·基尔回来找黛博拉·温格那样。

1656
01:24:33.850 --> 01:24:35.990
And that is exactly what it is.
没错，就是那样。

1657
01:24:36.170 --> 01:24:40.410
I really wish Rain had picked Steve up and told him around.
我真希望雷恩当时能把史蒂夫抱起来转圈。

1658
01:24:40.650 --> 01:24:42.070
I wish that had been in the script.
我希望剧本里能有这一出。

1659
01:24:42.330 --> 01:24:45.130
Well, Rain is Debra Winger in this scenario.
好吧，在这个场景里雷恩就是黛博拉·温格。

1660
01:24:45.490 --> 01:24:47.590
I know, but he's bigger than Steve.
我知道，但他比史蒂夫壮实。

1661
01:24:47.890 --> 01:24:54.190
So I think it would be like, that's how they, instead of them disappearing, like with him
所以我认为应该是这样，而不是像剧中那样他脱掉史泰博的制服，

1662
01:24:54.190 --> 01:24:58.450
taking his Staples uniform off, that he just carries Michael out.
而是他直接把迈克尔抱了出去。

1663
01:24:58.850 --> 01:24:59.250
Anyway.
总之。

1664
01:25:00.070 --> 01:25:04.150
Well, speaking of his uniform, when Dwight comes back to the party at Dunder Mifflin, he's
说到他的制服，当德怀特回到邓德·米夫林的派对时，他穿的是

1665
01:25:04.150 --> 01:25:06.550
wearing a Battlestar Galactica sweatshirt, right?
一件《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》的卫衣，对吧？

1666
01:25:07.210 --> 01:25:07.710
Yeah.
是的。

1667
01:25:07.990 --> 01:25:09.990
Okay, you know what about this?
好吧，你知道这事儿吗？

1668
01:25:10.110 --> 01:25:14.150
That Battlestar Galactica did not have any sweatshirt merchandise.
《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》根本没有出过任何卫衣周边。

1669
01:25:14.530 --> 01:25:15.410
Isn't that insane?
这不是很疯狂吗？

1670
01:25:16.130 --> 01:25:16.610
Yeah.
确实。

1671
01:25:16.690 --> 01:25:22.970
So our wardrobe designer, Carrie Bennett, had to make up a Battlestar Galactica merch sweatshirt
所以我们的服装设计师凯莉·贝内特不得不专门制作了一件《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》的周边卫衣

1672
01:25:22.970 --> 01:25:23.950
for Dwight to wear.
给德怀特穿。

1673
01:25:24.570 --> 01:25:25.890
Yes, they made it special.
是的，那是特制的。

1674
01:25:25.890 --> 01:25:27.010
It doesn't exiSt.
它在现实中并不存在。

1675
01:25:28.410 --> 01:25:31.030
I texted Rain and asked him if he still has it.
我给雷恩发了短信，问他是否还留着那件衣服。

1676
01:25:31.510 --> 01:25:33.090
Oh, please tell me he said he did.
噢，快告诉我他说是的。

1677
01:25:33.270 --> 01:25:33.990
He doesn't.
他没有。

1678
01:25:34.110 --> 01:25:36.350
And he super regrets not snatching it.
而且他非常后悔当时没把它顺走。

1679
01:25:36.530 --> 01:25:38.390
Oh, that would have been a good one to snatch.
噢，那确实是一件值得顺走的宝贝。

1680
01:25:38.530 --> 01:25:39.030
I know.
我知道。

1681
01:25:39.370 --> 01:25:39.870
I know.
我知道。

1682
01:25:39.870 --> 01:25:40.750
Someone has it.
肯定有人拿走了。

1683
01:25:40.910 --> 01:25:41.970
It's the one and only.
那是独一无二的。

1684
01:25:42.490 --> 01:25:48.130
Well, you know, when Dwight comes back in the office, I remember I have this moment where
嗯，你知道，当德怀特回到办公室时，我记得当时我正和奥斯卡说话，格雷格说，当他走进房间时，

1685
01:25:48.130 --> 01:25:54.090
I'm talking to Oscar and Greg was like, when he walks in the room.
我希望安吉拉·马丁在那一刻能放下戒备。

1686
01:25:55.050 --> 01:25:59.370
I want Angela Martin in the moment to sort of let her guard down.
你知道，所以我当时毫不掩饰地看着他，眼里充满了爱意和喜悦。

1687
01:26:00.710 --> 01:26:07.970
You know, so I'm blatantly looking at him with such like love in my eyes and happiness.
而且，你知道，我们依然保持着矜持。

1688
01:26:09.530 --> 01:26:11.450
And, you know, we're still reserved.
我们只是握了握手。

1689
01:26:11.710 --> 01:26:12.790
We just shake hands.
是的。

1690
01:26:12.990 --> 01:26:13.170
Yeah.
是的。

1691
01:26:13.550 --> 01:26:13.610
Yeah.
是的。

1692
01:26:14.230 --> 01:26:19.670
But there's so much emotion like between the two of us and Michael's just oblivious.
但我们两人之间充满了情感，而迈克尔却毫无察觉。

1693
01:26:20.230 --> 01:26:22.310
But then you shake hands with him.
但你确实和他握手了。

1694
01:26:23.030 --> 01:26:25.250
You welcome him back with a handshake.
你用握手的方式欢迎他回来。

1695
01:26:25.850 --> 01:26:26.390
Yes.
是的。

1696
01:26:26.390 --> 01:26:29.410
Now, I need to ask you a question, Angela.
现在，安吉拉，我得问你个问题。

1697
01:26:30.210 --> 01:26:30.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1698
01:26:31.010 --> 01:26:32.550
Have you not been in touch?
你们平时没有联系吗？

1699
01:26:33.230 --> 01:26:36.950
I mean, you guys aren't seeing one another outside of the office.
我是说，你们在办公室之外没有见面吗？

1700
01:26:37.150 --> 01:26:40.770
You don't go to each other's homes, talk on the phone.
你们不去对方家里，也不通电话吗？

1701
01:26:40.770 --> 01:26:41.770
I think so.
我想也是。

1702
01:26:41.770 --> 01:26:43.810
But I think he was miserable at his job.
但我认为他在那份工作上过得很痛苦。

1703
01:26:43.930 --> 01:26:47.510
And I was the reason he wasn't at the job he wanted to be at.
而我就是导致他无法从事他心仪工作的罪魁祸首。

1704
01:26:47.690 --> 01:26:53.710
And to see him come back in the office and to know that he's back where he wants to be.
看到他回到办公室，知道他回到了他想去的地方。

1705
01:26:54.710 --> 01:26:57.410
And it's so layered what he did for me.
他为我所做的一切，意义深远。

1706
01:26:57.590 --> 01:27:03.270
And then the risk I took going to Michael, all of that emotion is playing out in that moment.
还有我为了他去冒险找迈克尔，那一刻所有的情感都在爆发。

1707
01:27:03.730 --> 01:27:03.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1708
01:27:04.110 --> 01:27:07.670
It's not that it's the first time you guys have seen each other in a month.
这不仅仅是因为你们一个月没见了。

1709
01:27:08.090 --> 01:27:10.590
It's that he's back where he belongs.
而是因为他回到了他该待的地方。

1710
01:27:11.210 --> 01:27:11.690
Yes.
没错。

1711
01:27:11.830 --> 01:27:14.210
And we both made sacrifices for each other.
我们都为彼此做出了牺牲。

1712
01:27:15.030 --> 01:27:15.510
Right.
对。

1713
01:27:15.630 --> 01:27:20.910
And so it sort of takes our relationship to this next place, I think, very subtly of like,
所以我觉得这让我们的关系以一种非常微妙的方式进入了下一个阶段，就像是，

1714
01:27:20.910 --> 01:27:26.410
he did that for me and I went out of my comfort zone and did this thing for him and he knows it
他为我做了那件事，我也走出了舒适区为他做了这件事，他知道，

1715
01:27:26.410 --> 01:27:27.330
and I know it.
我也知道。

1716
01:27:27.550 --> 01:27:27.690
Right.
对。

1717
01:27:27.950 --> 01:27:28.990
So I think it's that.
所以我认为是这样。

1718
01:27:29.150 --> 01:27:33.570
But of course, Michael's oblivious and we look at each other with love in our eyes and shake hands
但当然，迈克尔对此一无所知，我们深情地对视一眼，握了握手，

1719
01:27:33.570 --> 01:27:34.550
and then that's it.
然后就结束了。

1720
01:27:34.730 --> 01:27:36.950
The party is well underway though, lady.
不过派对进行得很顺利，女士。

1721
01:27:37.290 --> 01:27:37.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1722
01:27:37.450 --> 01:27:41.330
Like while we're shaking hands and doing all this, everyone's having a good time.
就在我们握手做这些事的时候，大家玩得很开心。

1723
01:27:41.830 --> 01:27:46.830
And Jenna, we have a fantastic Phyllis dance catch.
还有珍娜，我们捕捉到了菲利斯一段精彩的舞蹈。

1724
01:27:47.090 --> 01:27:47.510
Yes.
没错。

1725
01:27:48.010 --> 01:27:51.010
Michael says to Pam, hey, Pam, shake yours and I'll shake.
迈克尔对帕姆说，嘿，帕姆，你扭一扭，我也扭一扭。

1726
01:27:51.070 --> 01:27:51.810
And she's like, no.
她说，不。

1727
01:27:52.390 --> 01:27:52.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1728
01:27:52.830 --> 01:27:52.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1729
01:27:53.010 --> 01:27:53.650
I'm not going to do that.
我才不要那样做。

1730
01:27:53.750 --> 01:27:56.050
But guess who's so like delighted?
但你猜谁特别高兴？

1731
01:27:56.710 --> 01:27:59.370
Phyllis at 25 minutes, 18 seconds.
25分18秒时的菲利斯。

1732
01:27:59.670 --> 01:28:05.350
You guys know that Phyllis was a burlesque dancer and you are seeing a straight up real
你们知道菲利斯以前是滑稽剧演员吧，你们在背景里看到的可是菲利斯跳的

1733
01:28:05.350 --> 01:28:09.110
deal burlesque shimmy in the background by Phyllis.
货真价实的滑稽剧抖肩舞。

1734
01:28:09.230 --> 01:28:11.510
I'll tell you what, that shimmy was not in the script.
我跟你说，那段抖肩舞剧本里可没有。

1735
01:28:12.330 --> 01:28:13.330
Oh, of course not.
哦，当然没有。

1736
01:28:13.330 --> 01:28:17.630
So I don't know where we got that, but I think Phyllis.
所以我不知道那是哪来的，但我认为是菲利斯。

1737
01:28:17.650 --> 01:28:19.850
I think Phyllis just improvised that in the moment.
我觉得菲利斯当时就是即兴发挥的。

1738
01:28:19.850 --> 01:28:21.950
Any chance to dance, Phyllis is in.
只要有机会跳舞，菲利斯绝对会参与。

1739
01:28:22.530 --> 01:28:23.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1740
01:28:23.190 --> 01:28:28.990
But also, I just want to say, Angela, I want to point out this party's going great that
不过安吉拉，我还要说一句，我想指出这场派对办得真棒，

1741
01:28:28.990 --> 01:28:30.310
Angela didn't plan.
而这并不是安吉拉策划的。

1742
01:28:30.750 --> 01:28:31.350
That's all.
我只是想说这个。

1743
01:28:32.230 --> 01:28:32.970
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1744
01:28:32.970 --> 01:28:33.890
She was there.
她当时也在场。

1745
01:28:33.890 --> 01:28:37.050
She was just sort of zoned out, but she was part of the planning.
她只是有点走神，但她确实参与了策划。

1746
01:28:37.050 --> 01:28:40.790
I know, but it's just maybe we should take note of what a great party it is.
我知道，我只是觉得我们或许该注意一下这场派对有多棒。

1747
01:28:40.850 --> 01:28:41.770
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1748
01:28:42.690 --> 01:28:43.610
Oh, my God.
我的天。

1749
01:28:43.870 --> 01:28:46.530
Well, I titled the next scene, Oof.
好吧，我把下一场戏命名为“哎哟”。

1750
01:28:47.310 --> 01:28:48.590
We have another oof?
我们又有一个“哎哟”了吗？

1751
01:28:49.450 --> 01:28:51.170
The scene is just called Oof.
这一幕就叫“哎哟”。

1752
01:28:51.670 --> 01:28:54.530
This was Heartbreak in the Break Room, was titled Oof.
这集原本叫“休息室里的心碎”，后来改名叫“哎哟”。

1753
01:28:55.490 --> 01:28:57.930
This is Heartbreak in the Conference Room.
这一幕是“会议室里的心碎”。

1754
01:28:58.130 --> 01:28:58.470
Yeah.
没错。

1755
01:28:58.670 --> 01:29:00.230
So here's what happens, you guys.
事情是这样的，各位。

1756
01:29:00.870 --> 01:29:03.690
Karen and Jim, they're sitting side by side in the conference room.
凯伦和吉姆并排坐在会议室里。

1757
01:29:04.390 --> 01:29:06.770
They're not even talking or looking at each other.
他们甚至没说话，也没看对方。

1758
01:29:07.010 --> 01:29:09.250
They're not even looking at each other.
他们连看都不看对方一眼。

1759
01:29:09.390 --> 01:29:14.970
That's even the saddest, like, oof part is that when he says he's still in the pan.
最让人心碎的“哎哟”时刻，就是他说他还陷在里面的时候。

1760
01:29:14.990 --> 01:29:16.090
He won't even look her in the eye.
他甚至都不敢直视她的眼睛。

1761
01:29:16.190 --> 01:29:16.430
Yeah.
没错。

1762
01:29:16.730 --> 01:29:18.230
She just gets up and walks away.
她直接起身走开了。

1763
01:29:18.370 --> 01:29:19.950
She's like, F this.
她心想，去他的吧。

1764
01:29:20.410 --> 01:29:20.850
Yeah.
没错。

1765
01:29:20.990 --> 01:29:23.190
Because she says, do you still have feelings for her?
因为她问，你还对她有感觉吗？

1766
01:29:23.750 --> 01:29:24.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1767
01:29:24.490 --> 01:29:26.530
And he says, yeah.
他说，有。

1768
01:29:27.510 --> 01:29:36.310
And I just want to say, Jim, yes, wishy-washy Jim is gone, and we have real Jim back again.
我只想说，吉姆，没错，那个优柔寡断的吉姆不见了，我们找回了真实的吉姆。

1769
01:29:36.470 --> 01:29:39.430
Jim is back, and he's owning his feelings.
吉姆回来了，他正视了自己的感情。

1770
01:29:39.650 --> 01:29:40.250
Yes.
没错。

1771
01:29:40.470 --> 01:29:41.090
We're happy.
我们很开心。

1772
01:29:41.390 --> 01:29:48.510
So this episode ends with Dwight, who thinks the party is for him, by the way, even though
这一集的结尾是德怀特，顺便说一下，他以为派对是为他办的，尽管

1773
01:29:48.510 --> 01:29:50.190
the sign says, welcome back, Oscar.
标语上写着“欢迎回来，奥斯卡”。

1774
01:29:50.870 --> 01:29:52.150
There's three signs.
有三条标语。

1775
01:29:52.330 --> 01:29:54.750
There's three signs that say, welcome back, Oscar.
有三条标语都写着“欢迎回来，奥斯卡”。

